              "text": "きっさてん (kissaten) is Sino-Japanese (kango): three Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are kis, \"consume, drink\" (Middle Chinese khek), sa, \"tea\" (drae) and ten, \"shop\" (temH) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
